# ─── Sensitive data ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Real phone number and street address live here. NEVER commit this file.
# The committed data/cv-*.yaml carry placeholders only, so nothing leaks even
# if this entry is ever removed by accident.
data/private.yaml
data/private.*.yaml
!data/private.example.yaml

# The signature scan for cover letters. Its path is named only in
# data/private.yaml, which is itself ignored - so no tracked file mentions it
# even by name, and a broken rule here still leaks nothing from git history.
assets/private/

# ─── Applications ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing under applications/ is tracked except the scaffold. A recruiter's
# name, email and phone are their personal data, an archived posting is someone
# else's copyrighted text, and the letter and tailored CV are drafts for one
# employer - none of it belongs in a history that outlives the application, or
# in a repository whose CV data also feeds a public website. Applications are
# archived locally. The scaffold is tracked so `cvforge new` works on a clone.
applications/*
!applications/_template/

# Your standing instructions, text snippets and learnings for Claude Desktop -
# written from these applications, so private for the same reasons. Here only
# when the repository is the home; normally they live in the home.
/guidance/

# `cvforge dashboard`: every application with its contacts and notes on one
# page. Here only when the repository is the home; normally it is in the home.
/dashboard.html

# ─── Editable diagram sources ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# draw.io exports embed their whole editable mxfile in a PNG metadata chunk.
# For one diagram that chunk was 12.8MB against 240KB of actual pixels, and it
# does not compress (9MB even zlib-9), so a tracked PNG is stripped and the
# editable original is kept alongside it under this name.
# Keep these files - they are how the diagrams get edited.
*.drawio.png
*.drawio

# ─── Generated artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# build/ may contain the resolved CV *with* private values merged in.
build/
out/

# ─── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ruff_cache/

# ─── Editors / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# ─── Per-machine settings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Written by `cvforge home set`: where this machine keeps private.yaml and the
# applications. A path on one machine is meaningless on another.
cvforge.local.toml
